---
import Headline from "../../shared/Headline.astro";
import Paragraph from "../../shared/Paragraph.astro";
import Wrapper from "../../shared/Wrapper.astro";
import Wysiwyg from "../../shared/Wysiwyg.astro";
import "./expect.scss";
---

<div class="speaking-expect">
  <Wrapper>
    <div class="speaking-expect-main-title">
      <Headline ele="h2" hlstyle="two"
        >Four Options for Signature Customizable Talks | 1 hour + Q&amp;A</Headline
      >
    </div>
    <div class="speaking-expect-left">
      <div class="speaking-expect-left-title">
        <Headline ele="h2" hlstyle="two"
          >5 WAYS TO DRIVE YOUR ORGANIZATION<br /> BY TELLING STORIES
        </Headline>
      </div>
      <div class="speaking-expect-left-content">
        <Paragraph>
          A rally cry for founders, marketers, and teams on how to build
          culture, marketing, and customer experience around a single compelling
          narrative.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>In this keynote you will learn: </Paragraph>
        <Wysiwyg>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Why storytelling is the most powerful way to communicate your
              business vision
            </li>
            <li>
              How to clarify your organization’s core narrative so customers
              understand what you stand for
            </li>
            <li>
              Ways to align culture, marketing, and customer experience around
              one compelling story
            </li>
            <li>
              A practical worksheet to start refining your organization’s story
            </li>
          </ul>
        </Wysiwyg>
      </div>
      <div class="speaking-expect-left-title">
        <Headline ele="h2" hlstyle="two"
          >MARKETING ISN’T ABOUT NOISE.<br /> IT’S ABOUT ACTION</Headline
        >
      </div>
      <div class="speaking-expect-left-content">
        <Paragraph
          >Let’s break down how to move people from passive observers to
          passionate, raving fans. When customers feel understood and part of
          something bigger than themselves, they don’t just buy — they advocate
          for you and that’s where real growth happens for your business.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>In this keynote you will learn: </Paragraph>
        <Wysiwyg>
          <ul>
            <li>
              How to move people from observers to engaged customers, building a
              community of customers who advocate for your brand through fandom
            </li>
            <li>
              Why emotional connection drives real business growth, focused
              marketing to solve real customer problems
            </li>
            <li>
              A simple worksheet and framework to turn attention into action
            </li>
          </ul>
        </Wysiwyg>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="speaking-expect-right">
      <div class="speaking-expect-right-content">
        <div class="speaking-expect-right-title">
          <Headline ele="h2" hlstyle="two"
            >DESIGN THAT SPEAKS | TURNING YOUR WEBSITE<br /> INTO A STORYTELLING
            MACHINE</Headline
          >
        </div>
        <div class="speaking-expect-right-content-inner">
          <Paragraph
            >Your company is unique, and your website shouldn’t feel forgettable
            or cookie cutter. Suzy will walk you through philosophies for
            mastering the storytelling perspective. Turning your website into a
            storytelling machine is the plot twist your business needs.
          </Paragraph>
          <Paragraph>In this keynote you will learn: </Paragraph>
          <Wysiwyg>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Why your website is your most important 24/7 storyteller and
                sales tool
              </li>
              <li>
                How to structure your website like a narrative that guides
                visitors to action
              </li>
              <li>
                Design and messaging strategies that make your site memorable
                instead of generic using key elements of storytelling-driven
                user experience
              </li>
            </ul>
          </Wysiwyg>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="speaking-expect-right-content">
        <div class="speaking-expect-right-title">
          <Headline ele="h2" hlstyle="two"
            >BRANDING | <br />ALL ABOUT MAKING PEOPLE FEEL SOMETHING</Headline
          >
        </div>
        <div class="speaking-expect-right-content-inner">
          <Paragraph
            >Let’s explore how to build story-driven branding that speaks to the
            heart — not just the eyes. A brand is so much more than a logo or
            design system. It’s the emotion you create, the clarity you bring,
            and the connection you build.
          </Paragraph>
          <Paragraph>In this keynote you will learn: </Paragraph>
          <Wysiwyg>
            <ul>
              <li>
                Why branding is about emotion and connection, not just logos and
                visuals
              </li>
              <li>
                How to build a brand story that clearly communicates who you
                help and why it matters
              </li>
              <li>
                The role of authenticity and consistency in building trust with
                customers
              </li>
            </ul>
          </Wysiwyg>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Wrapper>
</div>
